<newsitem itemid="223823" id="root" date="1996-11-28" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: United Utilities H1 pretax profit rises.</title>
<headline>United Utilities H1 pretax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence) (adjusted) 39.9		   vs 38.0</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 12.0		   vs 9.27</p>
<p> Pretax		     223.9		  vs 167.0</p>
<p> Turnover		   1221.5		 vs 531.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 220 to 249 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 294.3		  vs 185.2</p>
<p> Exceptional		nil		    vs 7.2 gain</p>
<p> Interest		   67.6		   vs 26.5</p>
<p> Tax			  15.0		   vs 11.4</p>
<p> Net taxed		  208.9		  vs 155.6</p>
<p> Transfer to reserves   146.1		  vs 107.4</p>
<p> Pay date		   February 13, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  December 17</p>
<p> Ex-div date		December 9</p>
<p>Note - United Utilities Plc is a multi-utility formed when North West Water took over regional electricity company Norweb last year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
